        <h2>Purchasing in Live Shows</h2>
        <p>First things first: You must have a payment method and shipping address added to your account in order to make purchases in a live show. Learn more about <a href="#">payment methods</a> and <a href="#">shipping</a>.</p>

        <h3>In-Show Buying Formats</h3>
        <p>Sellers on Lively feature three distinct buying formats when running items in a live show, depending on how they want to display an item or run a transaction.</p>

        <h4>Auction</h4>
        <p>This is exactly what it sounds like. A host will run an item as an auction where they dictate the starting price and duration. As higher bids are placed sequentially, you can choose to join the auction and place the next highest bid, assuming you meet the previous bidder's threshold and are willing to pay the price you entered.</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Standard Auctions:</strong> Items auctioned one at a time, awarded to the winning bidder. </li>
            <li><strong>Sudden Death Auctions:</strong> Very quick intervals where bidders must act fast.</li>
        </ol>

        <h4>Buy It Now</h4>
        <p>Buy It Now (BIN) is a fixed-price item that a seller has listed for purchase. This means there is not an auction happening for the item, just a direct Buy button. If you are the first to hit BIN and confirm your payment, you get it.</p>
        
        <h4>Flash Sale</h4>
        <p>Sellers may set up flash sales for items that are abundant so multiple users can purchase at a set price simultaneously during a live show window.</p>

        <h4>Giveaway</h4>
        <p>Giveaways on Lively allow sellers to run free item events or rewards. Buyers can enter a giveaway while it's running via the Giveaway tab.</p>

        <h2>Purchasing Outside of Shows</h2>
        <p>In addition to live streams, you can also purchase on Lively outside of shows via Marketplace listings. Sellers list items statically, much like a traditional store.</p>

